Camera feeds and Fiote vision contracts (@ws-contract-camera-vision: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @workspace-contracts, #requires @ws-camera-feeds, #requires @ws-vision-tasks, #requires @ws-observed-models) { r_610TE4GGKG9W0A5QA4B6NRPCVJ
Status: Pending. Owner refinement, 2026-11-15: a generic schema/plugin path connects a camera, its metadata and its place in the world to Fiote, which can apply an implemented vision model, watch chosen events or model the place once/periodically. Saving the actual video is outside this scope.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) owns scheduling. [Camera feeds](../features/Camera-Feeds.lingua) owns CFE.T01–CFE.T04; [Vision tasks](../features/Vision-Tasks.lingua) owns VSN.T01–VSN.T04; [Observed models](../features/Observed-Models.lingua) owns OMD.T01–OMD.T04. This contract extends F10 with concrete providers and composed acceptance; it does not build a global source catalog, require Argos or select a research reconstruction system.

## Native workflow and milestones

Select a place/component → Add camera through a supported source/plugin → inspect/adjust its location, orientation and image metadata → Inspect once, Watch events, Model once or Update periodically → inspect/stop the task and its outputs. Fiote uses the same scoped operations and actual media inputs. A source remains useful without a model provider, and a vision model can be replaced by another compatible implementation without changing the camera/place identity.

- [ ] **CV.M01.** Attach two independently supplied camera sources through one descriptor/stream interface, inspect their pose/resolution/calibration, view them and save metadata without archiving video.
- [ ] **CV.M02.** Pass actual frames and metadata to a supported vision model through native/Fiote task operations; inspect once and watch a defined event with bounded cost and explicit coverage.
- [ ] **CV.M03.** Generate and inspect an observed 2D/calibrated 3D representation once, then update its derived layer periodically from changed observations while preserving authored source.
- [ ] **CV.M04.** Handle multi-source time/pose quality, missing frames, source changes, stale jobs, cancellation and permissions without invented current state, unbounded work or retained raw video.

## Source and observation schema

- [ ] **CV.R01 — Generic providers.** Extend existing plugin manifests/provider operations and typed source/asset descriptors. A provider advertises discovery/description and its supported open/request/subscribe/update/close operations, formats and limits. Configured local/network cameras and plugin-produced sources use the same consumer contract. Keep source identity, view/stream identity, place association and transport credentials separate; replacing an endpoint does not replace the observed place. Provider-specific extras remain namespaced. No aggregator schema, subscription, public-camera catalog or additional hardware is required for the core proof.
- [ ] **CV.R02 — Explicit spatial and optical metadata.** Persist the descriptor fields below using existing quantity/frame/provenance types. Validate supplied metadata and distinguish absent, unknown, estimated and calibrated values. A camera's physical anchor, its optical pose, the observed footprint and the target model are distinct. Preserve their relationship through parent movement and floating-origin/view-scale changes. Imported metadata never grants camera control or starts a task.

| Field group | Required meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Identity and target | Stable source/provider/camera/view IDs; descriptor revision; associated place/component and parent frame; access/credential references outside public metadata. |
| Pose and frames | Position and orientation relative to a named frame; units, optical forward/up axes, handedness and pose convention; geographic/vertical reference when used; time validity, uncertainty and static/moving/PTZ status. |
| Image and transport | Advertised and actual delivered width/height, pixel/encoding/color/depth format where supported, still versus video, cadence/rate and source status; explicitly supported transport adapter. |
| Calibration | Lens/intrinsic parameters or supplied field of view, distortion, calibration resolution/revision/provenance, camera-to-world relation and alignment error where known. No exact calibration inferred from a direction label. |
| Frame preprocessing | Actual crop, rotation, resize and pixel-coordinate conventions, mapping output coordinates to the original image; any required transformed intrinsics. |
| Time and coverage | Frame/sequence and stream generation; capture time or stream timebase, receive/processing time, synchronization quality/uncertainty, gaps, freshness and optional observed region/depth coverage. |
| Capability and cost | Available image/depth modalities, rate/size/window limits, authorization for processing and declared remote processing/retention behavior. |

- [ ] **CV.R03 — Metadata travels with the frame.** Each frame/window reference pins its source/view/sequence, actual image metadata, capture-time quality and applicable pose/calibration revisions. Passing only a URL or textual description does not deliver visual input to Fiote or its worker. Opaque leased media handles or bounded provider attachments carry actual image data without embedding it in ordinary Records/chat history. Changing resolution, crop, pose or calibration changes the relevant generation; consumers revalidate mappings. Multi-camera windows preserve every source's timing and validity, with a declared maximum skew or explicit unsupported alignment.
- [ ] **CV.R04 — Transient media, retained results.** Use only bounded volatile buffers for acquisition, decode, inference and short synchronization/model windows. Their byte/time caps, frame-drop policy and consumer leases are explicit. No raw video archive, automatic frame snapshots, disk spill, debug-image logging or raw-media autosave is part of this capability. Persist descriptors, task settings and permitted derived observations/model revisions with source/time/model/calibration provenance. A worker requiring durable frame history is unsupported under this profile. Remote processing follows existing delegated grants and disclosed retention semantics; the feed descriptor grants neither. Expired inputs may leave a useful derived result but cannot be advertised as replayable evidence. Synthetic/preexisting permitted test fixtures do not enable recording live user feeds.

## Vision tasks and modeled outputs

- [ ] **CV.R05 — Model-neutral task interface.** Native controls and Fiote can describe/choose supported sources and models, request actual frames/windows, inspect once, start/query/change/stop event watches and request one-shot/periodic modeling. A task identifies source(s), region/purpose/predicate, implemented model/operator/build, cadence/window/duration, required outputs, target layer and resource limits. Model capabilities are checked against input modality, calibration, coverage and latency needs. Fiote may orchestrate a specialist vision worker; continuous watching does not require a language-model call per frame. A real image-capable implementation and native workflow must pass; an empty plugin hook or deterministic stub alone is insufficient.
- [ ] **CV.R06 — Events and observations.** Outputs carry observed property/event, source frame/window IDs and times, model/parameter identity, scope, confidence or explicit unknown/uncalibrated confidence, coverage and coordinate meaning. Map pixel detections to world coordinates only through supported calibration/geometry, retaining assumptions and uncertainty. Bound event rates, duplicate suppression, trigger/hold/retrigger and watched-region semantics. Missed/late frames or an inactive watch imply incomplete coverage, not proof of no event. Inference publishes observations; emitting external commands or changing accepted operational balances requires its separate existing action contract.
- [ ] **CV.R07 — Model once and update periodically.** A modeling task can use one or multiple supported inputs and return typed 2D regions/semantic state, calibrated 3D proxies or implemented reconstruction products. Preserve the distinction between observed, estimated, inferred and authored content. One-shot work yields a bounded candidate/result; periodic work uses the same interface and can automatically publish valid results to its already authorized derived layer. Pin the target/source/calibration/model generations, reject obsolete completion and preserve manual source edits. Keep last valid state with freshness/coverage when input disappears. Occlusion is not deletion; a plausible unseen surface is not measured geometry. Supported splat/mesh output consumes its actual representation/registration adapter and independent proof.
- [ ] **CV.R08 — Lifecycle and resource policy.** Share an admitted source acquisition across permitted viewers/tasks. Source viewing, event watching and model updating have separate leases/cadences and output owners. A retained task can continue offscreen within its budget; a view closing or appearance LOD change cannot silently alter its required sampling. Define worker priorities, bounded queues/backpressure, periodic coalescing/skipped intervals, cancellation, revoked access, stale input and reconnect/restart behavior. Stop releases media references and workers, and no missed-period event burst occurs on reopen. Unsupported quality at the admitted budget is a diagnostic, not silently invented output.
- [ ] **CV.R09 — Native use and source authority.** Reuse selection/tree/inspector, numeric/spatial attachment, granted Agent context, job status, model variants and accepted undo/adoption. Keep metadata-only access distinct from access to pixels and from permission to send them to a remote model. Ordinary viewing and native editing remain available when Fiote/provider is offline. Preserve readable status, keyboard controls and the [edit-panel geometry requirement](../../../Lince.lingua). Persist no source secrets in portable/public descriptors. Maintaining a derived model under an existing task grant does not require a new approval on each update.
- [ ] **CV.R10 — Honest scope and dependencies.** Feed/schema work starts after Assets and Shared presence. Vision tasks additionally need Agent context; observed-model publication joins vision with verified Agent authoring/native geometry operations. None waits for Federation, global geography, a character, scientific recording or a chosen Gaussian-splat research method. Federation consumes the verified feed/watch providers; full core acceptance joins the complete bounded camera/vision workflow. Existing imported splats or a rendered simulated camera do not prove live external-camera inference. Later higher-detail reconstruction adapters preserve the generic interface and prove their own actual input/output support.

## Canonical fixture and acceptance

**CV.F01 — A supplied local place and two live producers.** Use a small known room/table/ground plane, a light/door state sequence and a moving simple object with independent expected states, timestamps and calibrated reference positions. One producer exercises the supported network-camera path used by or compatible with the recovered ESP demo; another plugin producer delivers a controlled stream through the same contract. Deterministic synthetic live generation makes acceptance runnable without recording a user feed or requiring physical equipment. Recover the actual ESP compatibility evidence separately when available. Exercise a real selected vision model against the known sequence, plus separately controlled fault cases. Freeze source rights, frame dimensions/rates, calibration/clock quality, skew, task/window/queue/byte counts and measured hardware limits before implementation; do not invent universal performance targets.

| Workflow | Owner and milestone | Required proof |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **CV.W01 — Attach and inspect a feed** | CFE.T01–CFE.T04; CV.M01 | Register both providers, attach to a place/component, set/inspect pose/resolution/calibration, view actual images and save/reopen descriptors. Show unknown calibration, correct transformed frames and absence of archived media. |
| **CV.W02 — Give Fiote a vision task** | VSN.T01–VSN.T04; CV.M02 | Fiote selects an implemented model, consumes actual frames plus metadata, inspects once and watches a specified event. Native controls inspect/change/stop the same task. Compare events and coverage with the independent fixture oracle, including missed and duplicate frames. |
| **CV.W03 — Model once and maintain a representation** | OMD.T01–OMD.T04; CV.M03 | Generate a useful 2D layer and calibrated 3D proxy, then publish at least two periodic updates from changed observations. Preserve authored geometry, target identity and source/model provenance; inspect via native controls and Fiote. |
| **CV.W04 — Keep bounds and recover** | All three providers; CV.M04 | Interrupt/degrade/revoke a source or model, change resolution/calibration, expire a frame, conflict with a native edit and exhaust a budget. Retain explicit stale/partial results, reject obsolete work, stop cleanly and verify that no raw-media archive or hidden queue remains. |
| **CV.W05 — Combine views without inventing certainty** | VSN.T03/OMD.T04; CV.M03/CV.M04 | Use two calibrated views, verify actual time alignment and shared frame, then skew/drop one or move a camera. Check declared spatial error/coverage and unsupported output; do not combine unrelated timestamps or invent missing views. |

- [ ] **CV.P01.** Validate descriptors/units/transforms and cross-provider interchange, then compare the real model's outputs against independent expected events/image-space or metric references. Preserve input-generation recipes and source/model settings; do not claim exact input replay after transient live frames expire. Inspect native metadata, task state, freshness, causes of failure and cancellation. Measure capture/receive/output age separately, error and missed-event behavior, throughput/drops, memory/queues and release. Audit saved files, logs and worker scratch paths for unintended raw media.
- [ ] **CV.P02.** Run CV.W01–CV.W05 together only after real provider handoffs, then replay through 15.T10/15.W09 in mixed core acceptance. Federation uses its separately permitted feed/watch views and does not gain source credentials or private pixels through geographic proximity. Preserve earlier model/authoring/authority/resource guarantees. Record implemented protocols/models, actual quality limits and remaining higher-detail adapters; all capability status remains pending until proved.
